# CleanScape icon style

When adding or updating marketing/feature icons on public pages, use this established CleanScape style — do not invent new custom SVG sticker drawings or switch libraries without being asked.

## Stack
- Prefer **Phosphor Icons** (`@phosphor-icons/react`) with `weight="duotone"`.
- Keep **lucide-react** for small UI chrome (nav chevrons, form controls, etc.), not for branded feature illustrations.

## Colour mix (duotone layers)
Colour the two SVG paths creatively with **purple, white, and orange** (CleanScape brand):
- Soft fill = `path:first-child` at full opacity (`!opacity-100`) with peach/lavender/white fill
- Linework = `path:last-child` with purple (`#312c79` / `#5b3d9e`) or orange (`#d4694a`)
- Vary the mix per icon (e.g. orange fill + purple lines, or lavender fill + orange lines, or white fill + purple lines)

Example classes:
```
[&_path:first-child]:!opacity-100 [&_path:first-child]:!fill-[#f0a888] [&_path:last-child]:!fill-[#312c79]
```

## White sticker outline
Apply a stylish white die-cut edge via stacked white `drop-shadow` filters, plus a soft brand shadow for lift. Reuse the same filter treatment used on the residential “Cleaning that works around you” icons — do not add gradient washes behind icons unless asked.

## Layout reference
Feature cards may place the icon bottom-right on a warm cream tile (see `components/marketing/residential/residential-cleaning-page.tsx` + `feature-icons.tsx`).
